- `bridge/` is a new Rust crate at the repo root, outside the pnpm workspace. It is
  not published. Its dependencies are `tokio`, `tokio-tungstenite` with `rustls`, and
  `futures-util`, and `rustls` as below. `fly.toml` and a `Dockerfile` sit beside it. `fly.toml` names the app
  `rafters-mail-bridge`, region `sjc` (`sea` refuses new machines), and one service,
  port 993, handlers `["proxy_proto", "tls"]`, internal port 1143, with `[env] PORT = "1143"` and `TARGET_URL = "wss://mail-example-imap.ezmode.workers.dev/imap"`. `tokio-tungstenite` uses the feature `rustls-tls-webpki-roots`, so the image needs no CA bundle. `rustls` is a direct dependency, `default-features = false, features = ["ring"]`: neither tungstenite crate selects a crypto provider, and without one every `wss://` connection panics, while every loopback `ws://` test passes.
